---
/**
 * The just-yt logo: the name, and nothing else.
 *
 * There is no mark. A play triangle borrows YouTube's iconography, and an
 * abstract letterform next to a four-word sidebar is decoration standing in for
 * a brand. The package is called `just-yt`; setting that well is the logo.
 *
 * It is set in one weight and one colour. Splitting `just-` off in grey made
 * the wordmark read as two things — a qualifier and a product — when it is one
 * package name, and one that people type in full.
 */
---

<span class="logo">just-yt</span>

<style>
  .logo {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    /* Tight, because the hyphen already puts a gap in the middle of the word. */
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
</style>
